{title: Lived in Jerusalem}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 8:32; 9:38; 8:29–33; 9:35–39; 2 Samuel 13:3–32; 21:21}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In Jerusalem with their relatives
[Cm]Opposite their kinsmen in Jerusalem
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]Along with their kinsmen they stayed there
The register names [Cm]them in the tribal hall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Lived in Jerusa[Gm]lem with their relatives
Opposite their kinsmen [Cm]in the city
[Gm]Mikloth was the father of Shimeam
Near their kinsmen [Cm]in the holy [D]land
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Jeiel the father of Gibeon lived there
His wife was named Maacah [Cm]in the place
[Gm]Abdon was firstborn then Zur and Kish
Ner fathered Kish [Cm]and Kish fathered Saul
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Jonathan son of Shimeah struck him down
When he taunted Israel in the [Cm]fight
Shimeah was the [Gm]brother of David
And his son was shrewd in the [Cm]king's [D]court
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Mikloth fathered Shimeah
Lived opposite their [Cm]kins[D][Gm]men
{end_of_verse}
